comments:
By the way, in my original issue description, I said it looks like this started around 9/4, but after a closer look it seems that is not the case. I went back in the old builds around that time, and it seems there was [another error that occurred before that](https://prow.k8s.io/view/gs/kubernetes-jenkins/logs/ci-ingress-gce-e2e/1301675463063638017), `Error waiting for all pods to be running and ready: 1 / 20 pods in namespace "kube-system" are NOT in RUNNING and READY state in 10m0s` in the BeforeSuite.  So maybe that error got fixed, but then it made it farther and ran into this error.

I'm guessing the underlying problem has been around a long time as it looks like the job has been failing for one reason or another for as far back as I looked.

@rikatz thanks for the PR! :+1:
